                    <occupation>Attorney</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>EEd Pope note suggests: The first entry (4.3.1800) was probably John Shute
                            Duncan DNB 1769-1844 of 16 Lincolns Inn Old Square, attorney to the
                            Newhouses, Charlotte Smith's daughter and son-in-law (see Collected
                            Letters of Charlotte Smith). His brother Philip Bury Duncan DNB
                            1772-1863 was also of Lincolns Inn, both brothers in turn later became
                            keeper of the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford. </p>
